# Terraform/OpenTofu provider network mirror (T-P5-TFP): terraform and tofu init/apply a tiny configuration with one
# small provider (hashicorp/null 3.1.0, linux_amd64) through a Waystation mirror over TLS (both clients accept only
# https:// mirrors), with and without an API token in a credentials block; the mirror fetches through the provider
# registry protocol and verifies each SHA256SUMS signature (tests/clients/README.md;
# Documents/Operations/clients/terraform.md).

# The two origin registries (discovery, version lists, download documents), HashiCorp's release site (terraform's
# archive, SHA256SUMS and signature) and GitHub release assets with their redirect target (OpenTofu's).
HOSTS="registry.terraform.io registry.opentofu.org releases.hashicorp.com github.com release-assets.githubusercontent.com"
# Alpine with terraform, tofu, curl and the TLS front (compose.harness.yaml client-terraform).
CLIENT=terraform
NEEDS_STACK=1
# Two provider archives (about 4.6 MiB each: the smallest null release with plugin protocol 5 on both registries),
# their SHA256SUMS, signatures, download documents and version lists. Raised from the 8 MiB / 4 MiB defaults (a
# provider is a Go binary; no smaller real one exists).
FIXTURE_BUDGET_KB=11264
FIXTURE_FILE_MAX_KB=5120
